  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 3226.20 Fire Extinguishers",
  "priorExpiration": "2016-01-12",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 3226.20 Fire Extinguishers.\n\n(a) Pursuant to RSA 266:60-a, this section shall apply to the following motor vehicles:\n\n(1) All commercially registered motor vehicles with a gross vehicle weight in excess of 8,000 pounds, except municipally owned vehicles; and\n\n(2) All motor homes and motor home trailers that have motor vehicle registrations.\n\n(b) The motor vehicles listed in (a)(1) and (2) above shall be equipped with a fire extinguisher having an Underwriters’ Laboratories rating of 5 B:C or more that is in good working condition, securely mounted and in a readily accessible location to the driver.\n\nSource. (See Revision Notes at Chapter Heading Saf-C 3200) #8915, eff 6-22-07, EXPIRED: 6-22-15\n\nNew. #10886, INTERIM, eff 7-16-15, EXPIRES: 1-12-16; ss by #11016, eff 1-6-16",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c3200.html"
